$bold(c) dot (bold(a) times bold(b))$ is a signed volume: it is positive when $bold(a), bold(b), bold(c)$ constitute a right-handed set, and zero iff the three vectors are coplanar, that is, one is a linear combination of the other two. In $RR^2$, the analogous bracket $[bold(a), bold(b)] = epsilon_(i j) a_i b_j = a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1$ gives the signed area of the parallelogram formed by $bold(a)$ and $bold(b)$.
